NAME
    ps - list tasks

SYNOPSIS
    ps

DESCRIPTION
    List tasks with their pid, owner, name, state, heap use and capability
    count. Your own task is marked '*'. The flags column says, in words,
    whether a task is in the kernel, waiting on another task ("wait:N") or
    waiting for a notification.

SECURITY
    Which tasks you see is decided by your authority, not by asking: a
    login that is not the administrator sees only its own task. A task
    list is an information leak like any other.

SEE ALSO
    capview(1), whoami(1)
